meta {
  name: StartDemand
  type: grpc
  seq: 1
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.DemandService/StartDemand
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "project": { "id": "proj-1" },
      "external_key": "SUOPT-1315",
      "idempotency_key": "{{$guid}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0017, convention 5). The `ctx` field the messages still declare is ignored
  by the server — do not use it: it gives the false impression of scoping the
  call.

  It resolves the effective flow along the chain `platform ◁ account ◁ workspace ◁
  project ◁ demand` and **freezes the version** (ADR-0014). A change to a flow
  above does not affect a demand in flight.
}
